# This run reconstructs the graph from prepared.parquet and retrains the three
# architectures at their selected configurations, then runs the attribution
# analyses that the original `explain` stage could not complete (it was
# terminated on host memory exhaustion; o5.py reads features in 64-column
# blocks into a preallocated array instead of materialising the dense matrix).
#
# The retrained AUPRC differs from the reported figure by at most 0.0070.
# Retraining does not reproduce weights bit for bit: the scatter reductions
# underlying message passing are non-deterministic on CUDA. The figures
# reported in Chapter Four are those of the original run; this run evidences
# that they reproduce to within 0.007 on re-execution.
